                <pb facs="0640" n="528" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg528"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 24607/14 E.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Ambassador Reid.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-05-14"><hi rendition="#italic">May 14,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Reid is instructed to accredit the suite of Special Ambassador Roosevelt in
                    the following terms: Henry White, ex-ambassador, diplomatic delegate, with the
                    rank of envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary; Commander Andrew T.
                    Long, naval aid-decamp; and Maj. T. Bentley Mott, military aid-de-camp.</p>
            </div>
